1235	{"artifactId":"HLD-c2ba6fa62a148ed1","entry":{"id":"96005441","text":"Review history, 2026-10-11: nine daemon review rounds, with blocking findings of 7, 6, 4, 3, 2, 6, 1, 1 and 2. Every finding was corrected in this design; the corrections for the ninth round (the cross-file pass after a file event visiting pending rows that await the files just committed, with completion by id extended to imports; the start-up comparison removing a vector whose entity is gone) were NOT re-reviewed. One review attempt failed on the reviewer's side (17 premises against a template limit of 16) and recorded nothing. Stakeholder decisions recorded in this design: completeness as a separate field with the four status values kept; all three git ignore sources; tracked files indexed; generated or minified files and the .insrc directory left out everywhere; ambiguous relationships reported apart and not counted as incompleteness; the repository entity stored so that manifest dependencies are written. Findings of this depth are expected to continue in each Story's own design review.","actor":{"id":"legacy:subho-ghosh","kind":"person","properties":{"name":"Subho Ghosh"}},"timestamp":"2026-10-11T07:31:05.272Z","feedback":[],"kind":"comment"}}
669	{"artifactId":"HLD-c2ba6fa62a148ed1","entry":{"id":"be0336f7","text":"Amended after approval, 2026-10-11, on the stakeholder's decision: reindex is the one command and indexes every file from scratch, whether or not its content has changed; there is no separate repair. Today repo.reindex skips every file whose stored content hash is unchanged (src/indexer/index.ts:628 and :1004-1008). Not re-reviewed. Open for the stakeholder to confirm: unchanged text with an unchanged embedding model keeps its vector.","actor":{"id":"legacy:subho-ghosh","kind":"person","properties":{"name":"Subho Ghosh"}},"timestamp":"2026-10-11T07:43:12.990Z","feedback":[],"kind":"comment"}}
527	{"artifactId":"HLD-c2ba6fa62a148ed1","entry":{"id":"54f1f469","text":"Clarified by the stakeholder, 2026-10-11: a reindex calls the delete operations on the graph store and the vector store for the repository and builds everything again, vectors and document summaries included. This supersedes the earlier note that unchanged text keeps its vector. Not re-reviewed.","actor":{"id":"legacy:subho-ghosh","kind":"person","properties":{"name":"Subho Ghosh"}},"timestamp":"2026-10-11T07:46:08.679Z","feedback":[],"kind":"comment"}}
565	{"artifactId":"HLD-c2ba6fa62a148ed1","entry":{"id":"5d49450b","text":"Amended after approval, 2026-10-11, on the stakeholder's decision: while a repository is being indexed or reindexed, search and analyze requests about it return a named error that states the indexing state, and no partial answer. Carried by Story s5 (a new requirement and acceptance criterion ac4 in the definition). Not re-reviewed.","actor":{"id":"legacy:subho-ghosh","kind":"person","properties":{"name":"Subho Ghosh"}},"timestamp":"2026-10-11T07:53:00.827Z","feedback":[],"kind":"comment"}}
503	{"artifactId":"HLD-c2ba6fa62a148ed1","entry":{"id":"c29d060e","text":"Stakeholder decision, 2026-10-11: a reindex is queued at once, for a request and for the migration alike; only the repository being reindexed is offline, from the start of its own run until that run completes, and other repositories are answered as usual. Not re-reviewed.","actor":{"id":"legacy:subho-ghosh","kind":"person","properties":{"name":"Subho Ghosh"}},"timestamp":"2026-10-11T07:56:39.212Z","feedback":[],"kind":"comment"}}
722	{"artifactId":"HLD-c2ba6fa62a148ed1","entry":{"id":"0dcd0429","text":"Amended after approval, 2026-10-11, on the stakeholder's decision: Story s4 is reworded to the cause reproduced that day. The failure is not the semaphore limit: the daemon loses its file lock on the lock file when another descriptor on it is closed in-process, and another process that opens and closes the store then removes the semaphores. The title, the first and third criteria and the first requirement of s4 now speak of the store not being broken by another process. Not re-reviewed.","actor":{"id":"legacy:subho-ghosh","kind":"person","properties":{"name":"Subho Ghosh"}},"timestamp":"2026-10-11T08:16:16.235Z","feedback":[],"kind":"comment"}}
499	{"artifactId":"HLD-c2ba6fa62a148ed1","entry":{"id":"e7105cdb","text":"Stakeholder decision, 2026-10-11: the temporary allowance that lets the MCP server open the live store until Story s11 is kept, and its removal is a required part of Story s11 (a new acceptance criterion ac6, requirement and local constraint on s11 in the definition).","actor":{"id":"legacy:subho-ghosh","kind":"person","properties":{"name":"Subho Ghosh"}},"timestamp":"2026-10-11T09:27:55.718Z","feedback":[],"kind":"comment"}}
1188	{"artifactId":"HLD-c2ba6fa62a148ed1","entry":{"id":"592cddbb","text":"For Story s6 (stakeholder decision 2026-10-14: no separate issue, s6 addresses it). Concrete case in this repository: the bare-name ignore list for Node repositories contains 'build' (src/indexer/repo-type.ts:29), and hasIgnoredSegment (src/indexer/index.ts:104) matches it at any depth, so src/workflow/runners/build/ (19 files, all tracked by git; .gitignore has no rule for it, git check-ignore reports none) is never indexed. 19 files in src/ make 38 imports into it, all missing from the graph with the calls through them. s6's design should use this as an acceptance case: after s6, these 19 files are indexed and the 38 imports stored. It also affects Story s1's completeness until s6 lands: imports into that directory resolve to file ids that are never stored, so this repository reads not complete with them counted.","actor":{"id":"legacy:subho-insors-io-decision-recorded-by-the-controller","kind":"person","properties":{"name":"subho@insors.io (decision, recorded by the controller)"}},"timestamp":"2026-10-14T08:19:01.804Z","feedback":[],"kind":"comment","anchor":{"section":"src/indexer/repo-type.ts"}}}
1184	{"artifactId":"HLD-c2ba6fa62a148ed1","entry":{"id":"74e142f6","text":"CORRECTION to entry 592cddbb (2026-10-14): in THIS repository src/workflow/runners/build/ IS indexed. Its .insrc/config.json ignore list no longer contains 'build' (removed 2026-10-10), and resolveRepoIgnore (src/indexer/repo-ignore-config.ts:58-62) uses a repository's own list instead of IGNORE_DIRS, so the 38 imports into it are stored and Story s1's completeness is not affected. The defect stands for any repository on the default list: IGNORE_DIRS for Node contains 'build' (src/indexer/repo-type.ts:29, also 'dist' and 'out'; Python 'build'/'dist'; Java 'target'/'build'/'out') and hasIgnoredSegment (src/indexer/index.ts:104) matches it at any depth, hiding nested source directories that git tracks. s6 addresses it; use a nested tracked 'build' directory in a fixture repository as its acceptance case.","actor":{"id":"legacy:subho-insors-io-decision-recorded-by-the-controller","kind":"person","properties":{"name":"subho@insors.io (decision, recorded by the controller)"}},"timestamp":"2026-10-14T08:19:18.604Z","feedback":[],"kind":"comment","anchor":{"section":"src/indexer/repo-ignore-config.ts"}}}
